From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Add stateful partition path to preinstalled_images_paths

On WhaleOS/ChromeOS, Android images are pre-installed to the stateful
partition during image build (board_finalize_base_image copies them to
dev_image/share/waydroid-extra/images).  At runtime /usr/local is
bind-mounted from stateful/dev_image, so the images are accessible at
/usr/local/share/waydroid-extra/images.

Add this path to preinstalled_images_paths so waydroid init finds the
images without needing a symlink in the read-only rootfs.

--- a/tools/config/__init__.py
+++ b/tools/config/__init__.py
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
     "preinstalled_images_paths": [
         "/etc/waydroid-extra/images",
         "/usr/share/waydroid-extra/images",
+        "/usr/local/share/waydroid-extra/images",
     ],
